<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranavalona II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1883</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranavalona II was queen of the Merina kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> from 1868 to 1883. Married to the prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rainilaiarivony">Rainilaiarivony</a>, who held real power, she was baptised a Protestant in 1869, after which the royal idols were burned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> spread rapidly among the Merina. Her reign saw reforms of the law and schools before the first Franco-Malagasy War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranavalona-ii.jpg" alt="Ranavalona II" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranavalona_II,_photograph,_standing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
